meta {
  name: Billing Summary Grouped
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/billing-summary/grouped?statuses=ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED&groupBy=b2b
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  statuses: ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED
  groupBy: b2b
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
  ~referralPanelId: {{referralPanelId}}
  ~departmentId: {{departmentId}}
  ~categoryId: {{categoryId}}
  ~subCategoryId: {{subCategoryId}}
  ~branchLabTestId: {{branchLabTestId}}
  ~branchLabPanelId: {{branchLabPanelId}}
  ~paymentMode: CASH
  ~search: john
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Grouped Billing aggregate powering the Finance → Reports → Billing dimension
  panels. `groupBy` selects the dimension:

  Order-level (group whole orders):
  - **`b2b`** — by referral panel (B2B partner).
  - **`ref-by`** — by referring doctor.
  - **`internal-referral`** — by the **accession-transfer destination branch**. The
    dataset is re-sourced to orders whose sample was sent to another branch (an
    INTERNAL `SampleTransfer`), NOT the order's `internalReferralId`; money is
    order-level, each order attributed to its primary (oldest) transfer's
    destination branch.
  - **`external-referral`** — by the **external partner** of an EXTERNAL
    `SampleTransfer` (partner ref/name), same transfer-sourced model.
  - **`int-ref-user`** / **`ext-ref-user`** — by the internal / external referral
    **user** named in the order's Referral Details (`internalReferralId` →
    `InternalReferral.fullName`, `externalReferralId` → `ExternalReferral.name`).
    Distinct from `internal-referral`/`external-referral` (which now group by
    accession-transfer destination).
  - **`outsource`** — by the **outsource center** (`OutsourceCenter.name`) of the
    order's accession `SampleTransfer` (`kind=OUTSOURCE`), re-sourced like the
    referral transfers (each order → its primary transfer's center).

  Item-level (group the order's ALLOCATED lines; classification names resolved by id):
  - **`lab-test`** / **`lab-panel`** — by the stable **test/panel code**, so the same
    test/panel copied across pricing lists aggregates into ONE row (not one row per
    BranchLabTest/BranchLabPanel id). Panels group only panel lines; tests only test
    lines.
  - **`department`** / **`category`** / **`subcategory`** — by the line's test/panel
    classification, resolved as **branch scalar ?? master catalogue** (LabTest /
    LabPanel via `sourceLabTestId` / `sourceLabPanelId`), so lines whose branch copy
    is unclassified still classify from the master. Both tests and panels contribute;
    no individual test/panel rows. Panels have no sub-category, so `subcategory`
    matches tests only. A line with no classification anywhere is excluded.

  Returns an array — one row per group:

  ```json
  [
    { "id": "…", "name": "Acme Labs", "orderCount": 8,
      "gross": 0, "discount": 0, "net": 0, "paid": 0, "due": 0, "tds": 0 }
  ]
  ```

  Reconciles with `/orders/billing-records` and `/orders/billing-summary` for the
  same dimension + filters (Σ groups = Σ records = cards). For `b2b` / `ref-by` /
  `internal-referral` / `external-referral` the money is order-level (orders without
  that referral / transfer are excluded). For
  `lab-test` / `lab-panel` the money is the **allocated** test/panel-line money:
  gross = line unit price, order discount shared proportionally by net, paid fills
  the cheapest line first (ascending net, capped at each line's net), TDS shared
  proportionally by net, due = net − paid — so paid/due/tds are populated (not 0).
  `orderCount` = distinct orders. Amounts are integer minor units. Branch defaults
  to the active branch.
}
